n *ng-for=\"#thing of things\">{{thing}}, </span>',\n    directives: const [CORE_DIRECTIVES])\nclass HelloCmp {\n  List things = ['1','2'];\n}\n```\n\n<sub>output:</sub>\n\n```\nng-for: 1, 2, 1, 2,\n```\n\n<sub>version:</sub>\ndart: Dart VM version: 1.13.0-dev.7.10, (& 1.13.0-dev.7.12 )\nangular2: '^2.0.0-alpha.46',\n+angular2: Nov 13 17:13:47 2015, commit a31e2f5f4799e9ce20ae508f9f91dfeba05805f2\n+angular2: Nov 17 15:24:36  2015, commit 2c8fcec432ce352d6d514304445dd06a29aed364\n\nModified dart playground, hello, with ng-if, ng-for.\n\n```\n@Component(\n    selector: \"hello-app\",\n    viewProviders: const [GreetingService],\n    template:\n        '''\n        <div *ng-if=show>\n          once?\n        </div>\n\n        <div>\n          things: {{things}}<br/>\n          ng-for: <span *ng-for=\"#thing of things\">{{thing}}, </span>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"greeting\">{{greeting}} <span red>world</span>!</div>\n           <button class=\"changeButton\" (click)=\"changeGreeting()\">change greeting</button>''',\n    directives: const [RedDec,CORE_DIRECTIVES])\nclass HelloCmp {\n\n  bool show = true;\n  List things = ['abc','def'];\n\n  String greeting;\n  HelloCmp(GreetingService service) {\n    this.greeting = service.greeting;\n  }\n  void changeGreeting() {\n    this.greeting = \"howdy!!!\";\n  }\n}\n```\n\nresult, under Chromium, and in the generated JS output.\n\n```\nonce?\nonce?\nthings: [abc, def]\nng-for: abc, def, abc, def,\nhello world!\nchange greeting\n```\n","closed_by":{"login":"vsavkin","id":35996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vsavkin","html_url":"https://github.com/vsavkin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vsavkin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vsavkin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vsavkin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/us